From: SP11 X1E audio project
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 18:18:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 0024] ASoC: qcom: diagnose protected graph calibration frames

Diagnostic kernel only; do not merge into a daily kernel.

When the aggregate protected graph calibration returns AR_EUNSUPPORTED,
run the existing bounded per-frame diagnostic once per boot. This re-sends
each calibration record individually and reports how many SPF accepts or
rejects, identifying the first rejected instance and parameter.

The diagnostic is intentionally not passive and can delay first graph setup.
It does not change the normal aggregate return policy: AR_EUNSUPPORTED is
still ignored after the diagnostic, matching Qualcomm GSL behaviour.

This patch produced the 2026-07-31 result:

  frames=107 accepted=106 rejected=1 first-rejected=63
  iid=0x0000412b param=0x0800113d size=28 error=-EOPNOTSUPP

The experiment is complete. Preserve this patch for provenance; do not carry
it into the normal AUDIO VI kernel.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
index a52c51d..1f2a0be 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
@@ -1293,6 +1293,22 @@ int audioreach_send_protected_graph_calibration(struct audioreach_graph *graph)
 		 */
 		dev_warn(graph->apm->dev,
 			 "graph calibration returned AR_EUNSUPPORTED; continuing as Qualcomm GSL does\n");
+
+		/*
+		 * 2026-07-31 DIAGNOSTIC KERNEL ONLY. Do not merge into a daily kernel.
+		 *
+		 * Nothing has ever established whether SPF applies the supported
+		 * records of this aggregate or discards all of them. The frame walk
+		 * below answers that, but it is NOT passive: it re-sends each of the
+		 * ~111 records individually, costing that many extra SET_CFG round
+		 * trips during graph setup, which could stall bring-up on a slow DSP.
+		 * Guarded by sp11_frame_diag_done so it runs at most once per boot.
+		 *
+		 * Behaviour is otherwise unchanged: ret is still forced to 0 below,
+		 * exactly as Qualcomm GSL does.
+		 */
+		audioreach_diagnose_oob_frames(graph, cal, cal_size);
+
 		ret = 0;
 	}
 	if (ret) {
